From 6ac749b3626e8982a716f6636720168853cf3079 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:30:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] [TSReader] Seek to a key frame whose PES starts in the
 segment before

A PES can start at the end of one segment and continue in the next
segment. After the seek scan reads the next segment, the stream cannot
read the segment before again, so a seek to the key frame of that PES
went to the next key frame. The scan now copies the frames of a PES that
starts before the position where the read after the seek starts, and
the read starts with these copies: the key frame of the seek, and the
frames of the other streams from a PES that continues in the segment.
The scan keeps the frames of the last PES of the other streams for that.

The seek scan reads the frames left in the buffers at the end of a
segment. A video parser completes the last frame there at the end of
the data, so the rest of that frame in the next segment is not the
start of the next frame. The stream drops that data up to the next PES
with a PTS.

With video, only the video frames set the end time of the frames of a
segment, as only they set the seek position. A live seek that waits for
the next segment keeps the parsers, so the PES that continues from the
segment before is complete.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
